the above, we conclude the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$5{x}^{2}+7x+8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"20\">$=$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"70\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30\">$+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"50\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"25\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$x+3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$x+3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476880 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1d7da2ec-c6e2-53c6-957d-270bb7c7f62a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476880 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5x-8 \\\\  & x+3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,5{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}7x+\\phantom{0}8\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{5{x}^{2}+15x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-8x+8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-{8x-24}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $5{x}^{2}+7x+8$ by the linear binomial $x+3$ gives\n\n- the quotient $5x-8,$ and\n\n- the remainder $32.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}+7x+8}{x+3}=5x-8+\\frac{32}{x+3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476881 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476881 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37911" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476881 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476881 #edb/ref 1071 "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & 2x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+24x-8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\