b6-5a3a-99b2-d8098f93c67b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476894 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{2}$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n6{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}-4x+5\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}-6x+10 \\\\  & 2x+4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{3}+\\phantom{1}0{x}^{2}-\\phantom{1}4x+\\phantom{1}5\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,12{x}^{2}-4x+5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,12{x}^{2}-24x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,20x+5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{20x+40}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $3{x}^{2}-6x+10\\,$ and $\\,20x+5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476896 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476863 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476896 #edb/ref 1069 "q-113748" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476896 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476896 #edb/ref 1071 "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & 2x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+\\phantom{6}5x-\\phantom{6}2\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-9x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,14x-2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,19 \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476896 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4e550f33-edfe-5655-939e-8622636f2991" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476896 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\