\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,6{x}^{2}+2x+4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,6{x}^{2}-4x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6x+4}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are \n\n$\\,$ ${x}^{2}-2x+2\\,$ and $\\,-6{x}^{2}-4x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476900 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476900 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476900 #edb/ref 1069 "q-320867" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476900 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476900 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}-3x+2 \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{3}+\\phantom{0}{x}^{2}-\\phantom{0}x+11\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3{x}^{2}-x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-3{x}^{2}-3x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2x+\\,\\,2}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, we conclude the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"140\">$4{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-x+11$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"20\">$=$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"120\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30\">$+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"50\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"25\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"140\">$x+1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"50\">$x+1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476900 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5af2aa37-0f1c-5389-a626-d55c509b3ed3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476900 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}-3x+2 \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{3}+\\phantom{0}{x}^{2}-\\phantom{0}x+11\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3{x}^{2}-x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-3{x}^{2}-3x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2x+\\,\\,2}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $4{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-x+11$ by the linear binomial $x+1$ gives\n\n- the quotient $4{x}^{2}-3x+2,$ and\n\n- the remainder $9.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-x+11}{x+1}=4{x}^{2}-3x+2+\\frac{9}{x+1}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476910 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476787 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476910 #edb/ref 1069 "q-38074" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476910 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476910 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-14 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-2{x}^{2}-18x-\\phantom{1}1\\,\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-2{x}^{2}-4x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-14x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-14x-28}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{-2{x}^{2}-18x-1}{x+2}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476910 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6d7283af-f396-5468-82fb-4bc5cf7a26db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476910 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-14 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-2{x}^{2}-18x-\\phantom{1}1\\,\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-2{x}^{2}-4x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-14x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-14x-28}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $-2{x}^{2}-18x-1$ by the linear binomial $x+2$ gives\n\n- the quotient $-2x-14,$ and\n\n- the remainder $27.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2{x}^{2}-18x-1}{x+2}=-2x-14+\\frac{27}{x+2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476921 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476921 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37893" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476921 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476921 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+5x-3 \\\\  & 5x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,10{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}-10x-3\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{10{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,25{x}^{2}-10x-3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{25{x}^{2}+5x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-15x-3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,15x-3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{10{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}-10x-3}{5x+1}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476921 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "83ab4791-b4e2-54a9-99f4-adcd30bf75de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476921 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+5x-3 \\\\  & 5x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,10{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}-10x-3\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{10{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,25{x}^{2}-10x-3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{25{x}^{2}+5x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-15x-3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,15x-3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $10{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}-10x-3$ by the linear binomial $5x+1$ gives\n\n- the quotient $2{x}^{2}+5x-3,$ and\n\n- the remainder $0.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{10{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}-10x-3}{5x+1}=2{x}^{2}+5x-3+\\frac{0}{5x+1}=2{x}^{2}+5x-3.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476935 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476935 #edb/ref 1069 "q-114148" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476935 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476935 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+11 \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+\\phantom{1}8x-\\phantom{1}4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-3x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,11x-4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{11x-11}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{3{x}^{2}+8x-4}{x-1}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476935 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a96f6f0f-6a25-5d78-9b53-87a39a12c4cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476935 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+11 \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+\\phantom{1}8x-\\phantom{1}4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-3x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,11x-4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{11x-11}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $3{x}^{2}+8x-4$ by the linear binomial $x-1$ gives\n\n- the quotient $3x+11,$ and\n\n- the remainder $7.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}+8x-4}{x-1}=3x+11+\\frac{7}{x-1}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476938 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476938 #edb/ref 1069 "q-113730" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476938 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476938 #edb/ref 1071 "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & 2x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+4x+1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\